      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:2:15:2",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) إِنَّ النَّفْسَ إِذَا أَحْرَزَتْ قُوتَهَا اسْتَقَرَّتْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Abu Ali Al Ashary, from Abu Muhammad Al Zuhly, from Abu Ayoub Al Madainy, from Abdullah Bin Abdul Rahman, from Ibn Bukeyr, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘The soul, when it saves its foodstuff, is settled’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Abu Ali al-Ash’ariy has narrated from abu Muhammad al-Dhuhliy from abu Ayyub al-Mad’iniy from ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abd al- Rahman from ibn Bukayr from abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, who has said the following: “Abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that the Messenger of Allah O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause, has said, ‘When a soul reserves its sustenance it settles down.” "
        ]
      }
